---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Archex Studio — Identity into Interface"
  description="We help businesses build clear brands and better digital experiences, from first impression to interaction."
  path="/"
>
  {/* 01. Hero Section */}
  <section class="hero-field" aria-label="Identity-to-interface studio">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="hero-label meta">
          <span>Identity-to-Interface Studio</span><span>ARCHEX / STUDIO</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Identity <em>into</em> interface.</h1>
        <p>
          <strong>We help businesses build clear brands and better digital experiences.</strong><br />
          From creating your visual identity to designing websites and applications, we make it easier for people to understand, recognise and use your business.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button on-dark" href="/contact/">Discuss a design project</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="#disciplines">Explore our services</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="field-visual"
        data-resolving-field
        aria-label="Identity-to-interface visual"
      >
        <svg
          class="signal-path"
          viewBox="0 0 640 520"
          aria-hidden="true"
          focusable="false"
        >
          <path d="M24 430 C 145 390, 160 160, 300 210 S 450 370, 616 74"
          ></path>
        </svg>
        <div class="glass-note glass-note-a">
          Brand identity<br /><b>Point of view</b>
        </div>
        <div class="glass-note glass-note-b">
          responsive by design<br /><b>Desktop → mobile</b>
        </div>
        <span class="coordinate b">INTERACTION</span>
        <div class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>A</span></div>
        <div class="specimen">
          <div class="specimen-head">
            <span>Digital experience</span><span>Ready to explore</span>
          </div>
          <div class="specimen-main">
            <div class="specimen-word">Elegantly<br />designed.</div>
            <div class="specimen-lines" aria-hidden="true">
              <i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="specimen-foot">
            <span>Identity → use</span><span>Desktop → mobile</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="field-orbit field-orbit-a" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="field-orbit field-orbit-b" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 02. Two Design Disciplines */}
  <section id="disciplines" class="section section-rule shell reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">OUR DISCIPLINES</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Two sides<br />of one system.</h2>
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p>
          Brand identity and digital experience have equal weight. Creative
          direction is the connection between them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-grid">
      <article class="capability">
        <div class="eyebrow">01 / Brand Identity</div>
        <h3>
          Make it<br />recognisable.
        </h3>
        <p>
          Shape a clear point of view and a visual system people can recognise
          across the places your brand appears.
        </p>
        <div class="capability-list">
          <span>Brand strategy & positioning</span>
          <span>Logo & visual marks</span>
          <span>Typography & colour systems</span>
          <span>Brand guidelines</span>
        </div>
        <a class="capability-link" href="/capabilities/"
          >Explore Brand Identity <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        >
      </article>
      <article class="capability">
        <div class="eyebrow">02 / Digital Product Design</div>
        <h3>Make it<br />usable.</h3>
        <p>
          Plan and design digital experiences that carry that identity into
          clear, responsive, and intuitive everyday use.
        </p>
        <div class="capability-list">
          <span>Website design & UI</span>
          <span>Web & mobile application UX</span>
          <span>User flows & wireframing</span>
          <span>Design systems & tokens</span>
        </div>
        <a class="capability-link" href="/capabilities/"
          >Explore Digital Experience <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        >
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 03. What We Can Help With — Plain Language */}
  <section class="section section-rule shell reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">WHAT WE DO</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Services explained<br />in plain language.</h2>
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p>
          No agency buzzwords or design obscurity. Here is exactly what we
          design and why each piece matters to your business.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="services-plain-grid">
      <article class="service-plain-card">
        <span class="service-num">01</span>
        <h3>Brand strategy</h3>
        <p>
          Clarifying who you are, what you offer, and why it matters to your
          audience before making visual decisions. We uncover your core
          positioning so every design choice has purpose.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-plain-card">
        <span class="service-num">02</span>
        <h3>Visual identity</h3>
        <p>
          Designing your logo, typography hierarchy, colour palette, and
          visual rules to create a distinct, coherent market presence that builds
          immediate trust and recognition.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-plain-card">
        <span class="service-num">03</span>
        <h3>UI/UX design</h3>
        <p>
          Creating website and application layouts, user flows, and interaction
          patterns focused on clarity, speed, and ease of use so customers find
          what they need without friction.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-plain-card">
        <span class="service-num">04</span>
        <h3>Design systems</h3>
        <p>
          Building organised UI component libraries, design token
          specifications, and documentation so your digital products stay
          consistent as your team and business scale.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 04. Our Design Approach — 4 Principles */}
  <section class="section section-rule shell reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">PHILOSOPHY</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">How we approach<br />every design.</h2>
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p>
          Good design is not decorative flourish. It is clear thinking made
          visible through rigorous, intentional principles.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="principles-grid">
      <div class="principle-card">
        <span class="principle-num">01</span>
        <h4>Understand before designing</h4>
        <p>
          We ground every aesthetic choice in your business goals, target
          audience, and functional requirements before touching pixels.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card">
        <span class="principle-num">02</span>
        <h4>Audience-first interaction</h4>
        <p>
          We design for the real person using the screen, ensuring every
          interaction feels natural, immediate, and legible.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card">
        <span class="principle-num">03</span>
        <h4>Clarity over complexity</h4>
        <p>
          We strip away unnecessary ornament, confusing terminology, and visual
          friction to let your core value stand out.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card">
        <span class="principle-num">04</span>
        <h4>Design for implementation</h4>
        <p>
          We design with engineering reality in mind, producing clean specs and
          tokens ready for build in code without translation loss.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="section-footer-action">
      <a class="inline-link" href="/studio/"
        >Read our full studio methodology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
      >
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 05. The Design Process — 5 Steps */}
  <section class="section section-rule shell reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">WORKING METHOD</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">
        A clear, collaborative<br />design process.
      </h2>
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p>
          A structured five-step path from first conversation to final production
          assets, with transparency at every milestone.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="process-steps-list">
      <div class="process-step-item">
        <div class="process-step-num">Step 01</div>
        <div class="process-step-content">
          <h4>Understand</h4>
          <p>
            We learn about your business, target audience, competitors, and
            goals to establish a clear project foundation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="process-step-item">
        <div class="process-step-num">Step 02</div>
        <div class="process-step-content">
          <h4>Define</h4>
          <p>
            We outline project scope, user journeys, design requirements, and
            technical constraints.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="process-step-item">
        <div class="process-step-num">Step 03</div>
        <div class="process-step-content">
          <h4>Design</h4>
          <p>
            We explore visual directions, wireframes, and interface layouts
            through collaborative review cycles.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="process-step-item">
        <div class="process-step-num">Step 04</div>
        <div class="process-step-content">
          <h4>Refine</h4>
          <p>
            We polish typography, colours, interaction details, and edge cases
            based on structured feedback.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="process-step-item">
        <div class="process-step-num">Step 05</div>
        <div class="process-step-content">
          <h4>Deliver</h4>
          <p>
            We package production-ready design files, tokens, guidelines, and
            handoff documentation for your engineering team.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 06. Micro-CTA Bridge to Craft */}
  <section class="section section-rule shell reveal">
    <div class="craft-bridge-box">
      <div class="craft-bridge-content">
        <div class="eyebrow">NEED MORE THAN DESIGN?</div>
        <h3>Your design can become a working product.</h3>
        <p>
          Archex Studio focuses on how your brand and product look, feel, and
          function for users. If you need your website or software engineered,
          <strong>Archex Craft</strong> is our dedicated engineering practice that
          turns these designs into fast, reliable production code.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="craft-bridge-action">
        <a
          class="button on-dark"
          href="https://craft.archexweb.in"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Meet Craft — Software & Engineering <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 07. Studio Archive / Ecosystem Showcase */}
  <section class="section section-rule shell reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">STUDIO ARCHIVE</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Our first project.<br />Archex Craft.</h2>
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p>
          Archex Craft is our first project — an internal website designed for
          our engineering practice, demonstrating our complete
          identity-to-interface system. Explore the live website or view the
          project overview.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence">
      <div class="evidence-frame">
        <div class="evidence-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow">01 / First project</div>
          <h3>Archex<br />Craft.</h3>
          <p>The beginning of this archive.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <dl class="meta-list">
        <div>
          <dt>Project overview</dt><dd>
            <a href="/archex-craft/">View the project overview</a>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Created by</dt><dd>The same owner and team</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Live website</dt><dd>
            <a href="https://craft.archexweb.in" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Visit the craft website</a
            >
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="reserved-grid">
      <article class="reserved">
        <small>02 / Future position 01</small><strong>Future<br />work</strong
        ><small>Position reserved for a future project.</small>
      </article>
      <article class="reserved">
        <small>03 / Future position 02</small><strong>Future<br />work</strong
        ><small>Position reserved for a future project.</small>
      </article>
      <article class="reserved">
        <small>04 / Future position 03</small><strong>Future<br />work</strong
        ><small>Position reserved for a future project.</small>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 08. Studio FAQs */}
  <section class="section section-rule shell reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">
        Common questions<br />about working with Studio.
      </h2>
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p>
          Clear answers to understand how we collaborate, what we deliver, and
          how we help your business succeed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faqs-grid">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Can I hire Studio just for brand design without web design?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes. We frequently partner with businesses solely to establish their
          brand strategy, logo mark, typography system, colour palette, and
          brand guidelines.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Can I hire Studio just for digital product or UI/UX design?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes. If you already have established brand guidelines, we design
          websites, web apps, mobile interfaces, or scalable design systems that
          honour your existing brand identity.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What deliverables do you provide at the end of a project?</h3>
        <p>
          You receive organized Figma files, production-ready vector assets (SVG,
          PNG, web fonts), design token specifications, brand manuals, and
          developer handoff documentation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How does Studio collaborate with Archex Craft or external developers?</h3>
        <p>
          We design with engineering reality in mind. We provide explicit
          component states, responsive breakpoints, layout grids, and token
          values that frontend engineers can implement directly without guesswork.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 09. Closing CTA Band */}
  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="cta-inner">
      <h2>Have a brand or digital experience in mind?</h2>
      <p class="cta-subtext">
        Tell us what you're looking to create. We'll help you shape a clear
        identity and an intuitive product.
      </p>
      <a class="button on-dark" href="/contact/"
        >Contact <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
